# AppArmor Local Customizations

This directory contains local customizations for AppArmor profiles.
Files in this directory are included by the main AppArmor profiles
to allow for site-specific modifications without editing the main profiles.

## Usage:
- Add local rules to files matching the profile name
- Example: rules for /usr/bin/firefox go in local/usr.bin.firefox  
- Use include statements in main profiles: #include <local/usr.bin.firefox>

## Profile deployment:
- Profiles will be deployed post-installation using Victor commands
- Use: vic setup security apparmor
- Monitor with: vic run system security-status

## Security Best Practices:
- Only add rules you explicitly need for your development workflow
- Document why each rule exists with comments
- Review local customizations regularly
- Test profile changes in complain mode first: `aa-complain /path/to/profile`
- Use the most restrictive rules possible while maintaining functionality

## Common Development Scenarios:
- Debugger access: May require ptrace permissions
- Container development: Docker/Podman may need additional capabilities
- Network services: Local development servers may need network binds
- File system access: Development tools may need broader file access

## Troubleshooting:
- Check AppArmor logs: `journalctl | grep -i apparmor`
- Switch to complain mode: `aa-complain /path/to/profile`
- Generate profile rules: `aa-genprof /path/to/binary`
- Update profiles: `aa-logprof`

## Victor Integration:
- Security status: `vic run system security-status`
- AppArmor management: `vic setup security apparmor`
- Profile updates: `vic run security update-profiles`